Whisper's static pipeline on the NPU takes a prompt given when it's made

The static pipeline, which the NPU runs when STATIC_PIPELINE is asked
for, makes its first decoder take four tokens, the start of a
transcription, and refuses initial_prompt and hotwords, so words a
speaker uses that Whisper doesn't know can't be given to it there. (The
NPU's other pipeline can't take one either: the plugin fixes its first
step at four tokens.) A prompt given as a property when the pipeline is
made is now measured then, the first decoder is made long enough for it
and the start tokens together, and each take puts it before them as the
other pipelines do. A prompt given only at a take is still refused when
it doesn't fit.

